title: The Rote Fahne's Line
subtitle: Whoever writes the party paper's front page tells 200,000 members what the party thinks.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: rf_party
view-if: rf_editorial_timer <= 0 and party_banned = 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; rf_editorial_timer = 3

= The Rote Fahne's Line

[? if player_leads : As the leadership, you set the editorial line of the Rote Fahne. ?][? if player_leads = 0 : The leadership controls the paper, but your people write for it, and a well-placed article can still turn a district. ?]

- @united_front: The united front: an open hand to SPD workers.
- @offensive: The offensive: the crisis is revolutionary, prepare for power.
- @unity: Unity: the party's strength is its discipline.
- @moscow: The International: Moscow's lessons for the German party.

@united_front
on-arrival: {!
var w = Q.player_leads ? 1 : 0.5;
Q.right_strength += 5 * w;
Q.spd_relation += 5 * w;
Q.union_influence += 2 * w;
Q.left_dissent += 5 * w;
Q.right_dissent -= 3 * w;
!}

The paper calls on SPD workers to join the KPD in factory councils, price-control committees and defence units. Some SPD locals answer. The Left calls it begging.

@offensive
on-arrival: {!
var w = Q.player_leads ? 1 : 0.5;
Q.left_strength += 5 * w;
Q.readiness += 3 * w;
Q.spd_relation -= 5 * w;
Q.right_dissent += 5 * w;
Q.left_dissent -= 3 * w;
!}

The paper says what many members feel: the republic is finished and the question is who inherits it. Militants cheer. The SPD press quotes the article as proof that the Communists want civil war.

@unity
on-arrival: {!
var w = Q.player_leads ? 1 : 0.5;
Q.center_strength += 4 * w;
for (var f of window.RF.factions) {
    Q[f + '_dissent'] -= 3 * w;
}
!}

The paper prints a long appeal for party discipline and avoids the questions that divide the factions. Tempers cool, for now.

@moscow
on-arrival: {!
var w = Q.player_leads ? 1 : 0.5;
Q.stalin_strength += 3 * w;
Q[Q.player + '_moscow'] += 4;
Q.autonomy -= 2;
!}

The paper reprints the latest resolutions of the Executive Committee of the Communist International (ECCI) with a respectful commentary. Moscow notices who wrote it.
